IMPORT prelude

-- Taxation Administration Act 1953 (Cth) -- tax file numbers: who may ask for one and what may be done with it (s 2 definition,
-- s 8C(2), Part III Division 2 Subdivision BA, ss 8WA, 8WB); PAYG withholding (Schedule 1 Part 2-5): which payments must have an
-- amount withheld (ss 12-1, 12-10, 12-35, 12-40, 12-190), when and how much (ss 16-5, 15-10, 15-15), the administrative penalty for
-- not withholding (s 16-30), when the payer must pay it to the Commissioner (ss 16-75, 16-95, 16-100, 16-105) and the recipient's
-- credit (s 18-15); and PAYG instalments (Schedule 1 Part 2-10, Division 45): who is liable (ss 45-15, 45-50), what kind of payer an
-- individual is (ss 45-125, 45-130, 45-132, 45-134, 45-140, 45-155), when instalments are due (ss 45-60, 45-61, 45-70), the
-- applicable rate and the instalment on instalment income (ss 45-1, 45-110), notifying instalment income (s 45-20) and the credit
-- (s 45-30).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 226, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026 and Act No. 82, 2026),
-- register id C2026C00393, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1953A00001.txt (all four volumes in one file).
-- THE FORMULAS ARE MISSING FROM THE DEPOSIT: ss 45-110(1), 45-115(1)(a) and 45-320(1) end "as follows:" or "using the formula:" and
-- the text goes straight on. Where a formula is needed it is taken from the Guide (s 45-1) and labelled INFERENCE.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0015 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 5 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave scenarios: Chloe c020 (2018-03-14, turns 15: "Must a 15-year-old have a TFN? What is a junior rate?
-- Is super payable?"), c041 (2024-02-29, first payslip on $5,833.33 a month: "What is withheld?"); Jake k020 (2021-08-30, turns
-- 15: a TFN and no job yet), k043 (2028-10-20, first tax return as a sole trader on $31,000: PAYG instalments); Daniel d012
-- (2012-10-15, turns 16: a TFN and a casual job). The ledger names "Part VA (tax file numbers)" of THIS Act: there is no Part VA in
-- the deposited compilation. Part VA is in the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936 (ss 202-202HA, not deposited here); this Act's TFN
-- provisions are the definition in s 2 (which points to s 202A of that Act), s 8C(2) and Subdivision BA. SCOPED to those, Parts
-- 2-5 and 2-10 as the events ask, and the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Junior rates (Fair Work Act 2009 and the General Retail Industry Award) and superannuation (Superannuation Guarantee
-- (Administration) Act 1992 s 28) -- not this Act. ITAA 1936 Part VA (TFN declarations, issue of TFNs, s 202CB) -- not deposited.
-- The amount to withhold is set by the Commissioner's withholding schedules or by regulations (s 15-10): an INPUT, never a figure
-- here. The value of a penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA) -- an INPUT. The large withholder's weekday table (s 16-75(1)), the
-- Commissioner's withholder-status determinations (ss 16-110, 16-115), the June 2001 and wholly-owned-group limbs of ss 16-95 and
-- 16-100, s 8WC (investments), Subdivisions 12-C to 12-J, ss 12-45 to 12-60, Divisions 13 and 14, notional tax and the instalment
-- rate (ss 45-320 to 45-340, formula missing), GDP adjustment (Subdivision 45-L), benchmark tax (Subdivision 45-M), varying the
-- rate (Subdivision 45-F), monthly payers beyond the s 45-138 result (an INPUT), companies, trusts, partnerships and consolidated
-- groups, and the general interest charge.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers. Income years end on 30 June and are named by the calendar year in which they end.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive encodings (the
-- writing-l4-rules skill was not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human
-- gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Taxation Administration Act 1953 -- TFNs and PAYG`

§§ `s 2, s 8C(2), ss 8WA, 8WB -- tax file numbers`

-- s 2(1): "tax file number means a tax file number as defined in section 202A of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1936."
-- s 8C(2): "a person shall not be taken to have refused or failed to furnish information to the Commissioner or another person ...
-- merely because the person has refused or failed to quote the person's tax file number". No provision of this Act obliges an
-- individual of any age to obtain or quote a TFN; what not quoting costs is in the withholding schedules (s 15-1: a TFN declaration
-- "may affect how to calculate the amount to withhold").
GIVEN `failed to give other required information` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to quote own TFN` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person has failed to give information under s 8C` IF
    `failed to give other required information`

-- s 8WA(1): "A person must not require or request another person to quote the other person's tax file number." 100 penalty units or
-- imprisonment for 2 years, or both. (1AA): does not apply if "(a) provision is made by or under a taxation law ... for the person to
-- quote the number"; (b) in connection with exercising powers or performing functions under, or complying with an obligation imposed
-- by, a taxation law or listed Commonwealth law; (c) acting on the other person's behalf in the conduct of their affairs. (1A): a
-- request so that the number can be included in an application for an ABN. (2): requesting a document on which the TFN is recorded,
-- if the other person may remove it. (3): a statement the other person could reasonably understand as a request counts. (4): no
-- obligation to require anyone to quote a TFN.
DECLARE `TFN request` HAS
    `a taxation law provides for the number to be quoted to this person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in connection with a function or obligation under a taxation law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acting on the other person's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for an ABN application` IS A BOOLEAN
    `only asks for a document from which the TFN may be removed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `r` IS A `TFN request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `requiring or requesting the TFN is an offence under s 8WA` IF
        (NOT `r`'s `a taxation law provides for the number to be quoted to this person`)
    AND (NOT `r`'s `in connection with a function or obligation under a taxation law`)
    AND (NOT `r`'s `acting on the other person's behalf`)
    AND (NOT `r`'s `for an ABN application`)
    AND (NOT `r`'s `only asks for a document from which the TFN may be removed`)

-- s 8WB(1): must not "(a) record another person's tax file number or maintain such a record; or (b) use [it] in a manner connecting it
-- with the other person's identity; or (c) divulge or communicate [it] to a third person." 100 penalty units or 2 years, or both.
-- (1A): not "(a) to the extent required or permitted by, or reasonably necessary in order to comply with an obligation imposed by, a
-- taxation law" or listed Commonwealth law; (b) exercising powers or functions under such a law; (ba) a registrar under s 355-67(2);
-- (c) acting on the other person's behalf.
GIVEN `records, uses or divulges it` IS A BOOLEAN, `required or permitted by a taxation law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exercising a function under a taxation law` IS A BOOLEAN, `acting for the TFN holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dealing with the TFN is an offence under s 8WB` IF
        `records, uses or divulges it`
    AND (NOT `required or permitted by a taxation law`)
    AND (NOT `exercising a function under a taxation law`)
    AND (NOT `acting for the TFN holder`)

§§ `ss 12-1, 12-10, 12-35, 12-40, 12-190, 16-5 -- payments from which an amount must be withheld`

-- s 12-35: "An entity must withhold an amount from salary, wages, commission, bonuses or allowances it pays to an individual as an
-- employee". s 12-40: a company must withhold from remuneration paid to a director. Neither asks the employee's age, or whether a TFN
-- was quoted. s 12-1(1): need not withhold under 12-35 or 12-40 "if the whole of the payment is exempt income"; (1A): nor under
-- Subdivision 12-B or s 12-190 if the whole payment is neither assessable nor exempt income. s 12-10: the Division "does not apply to
-- a payment in so far as it consists of providing a non-cash benefit".
-- s 12-190(1): the payer must withhold from a payment for a supply made "in the course or furtherance of an enterprise carried on in
-- Australia by the other entity" unless an exception applies: (2) an invoice or other document quotes the supplier's ABN; (4)(a) the
-- payment is not made in the course of the payer's own enterprise; (4)(b) the payment (net of GST) "does not exceed $50 or such
-- higher amount as is specified in regulations"; (6) an individual's written statement that the supply is a hobby or wholly private,
-- unless the payer has reasonable grounds to believe it false. ((3), (4)(c), (d) and (5) are not modelled.)
-- s 16-5: "the entity must do so when making the payment."
DECLARE `Payment kind` IS ONE OF
    `salary or wages to an employee`
    `a commission, bonus or allowance to an employee`
    `remuneration to a company director`
    `a payment for a supply by a business`
    `a non-cash benefit`

DECLARE Payment HAS
    `kind` IS A `Payment kind`
    `the whole payment is exempt income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the whole payment is neither assessable nor exempt income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier's ABN is quoted on an invoice or document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in the course of the payer's enterprise in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payment net of GST` IS A NUMBER
    `the higher amount in the regulations, or 50` IS A NUMBER
    `the supplier gave a hobby or private-supply statement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payer has grounds to think that statement false` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `p` IS A Payment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payer must withhold` IF
    CONSIDER `p`'s `kind`
    WHEN `a non-cash benefit` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a payment for a supply by a business` THEN
            (NOT `p`'s `the whole payment is neither assessable nor exempt income`)
        AND (NOT `p`'s `the supplier's ABN is quoted on an invoice or document`)
        AND `p`'s `made in the course of the payer's enterprise in Australia`
        AND `p`'s `the payment net of GST` GREATER THAN `p`'s `the higher amount in the regulations, or 50`
        AND ((NOT `p`'s `the supplier gave a hobby or private-supply statement`) OR `p`'s `the payer has grounds to think that statement false`)
    OTHERWISE
            (NOT `p`'s `the whole payment is exempt income`)
        AND (NOT `p`'s `the whole payment is neither assessable nor exempt income`)

§§ `ss 15-10, 15-15, 16-30 -- how much, and the penalty for not withholding`

-- s 15-10(1): the amount Subdivision 12-B requires "is to be worked out under the withholding schedules made under section 15-25.
-- However, if the regulations prescribe how the amount is to be worked out, then it is to be worked out under the regulations." (2):
-- s 12-190 (Subdivision 12-E) amounts are worked out under the regulations. s 15-15: the Commissioner may vary the amount, including
-- to nil, by written notice or legislative instrument. s 15-30: the schedules must have regard to the income tax and Medicare levy
-- rates and the HELP repayment amounts (so a HECS component, c041, is in the schedule, not in this Act). The schedule or regulation
-- amount is an INPUT.
GIVEN `the schedule or regulation amount` IS A NUMBER, `the Commissioner varied it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the varied amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount to withhold` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner varied it` THEN `the varied amount` ELSE `the schedule or regulation amount`

-- s 16-30(1): an entity (except an exempt Australian government agency) that "fails to withhold an amount as required by Division 12
-- ... is liable to pay to the Commissioner a penalty equal to that amount." (The agency penalties in ss 16-35 to 16-43 and the
-- offence in s 16-25 -- 10 penalty units, strict liability -- are not computed.)
GIVEN `the amount required` IS A NUMBER, `withheld it` IS A BOOLEAN, `an exempt Australian government agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 16-30 penalty` MEANS
    IF `withheld it` OR `an exempt Australian government agency` THEN 0 ELSE `the amount required`

§§ `ss 16-75, 16-95, 16-100, 16-105 -- when the payer pays the Commissioner`

-- s 16-95(1)(b): a large withholder for a month if the amounts withheld "during a financial year ending at least 2 months before the
-- current month exceeded $1 million". s 16-100(1)(b): medium if not large and the amounts withheld "during a financial year ending
-- before the current month exceeded $25,000". s 16-105: small if "there is at least one amount withheld by the entity during that
-- month" and it is neither large nor medium. ("Exceeded": exactly $25,000 is not medium.) The June 2001, group and Commissioner
-- determination limbs are not modelled.
DECLARE `Withholder size` IS ONE OF
    `a large withholder`
    `a medium withholder`
    `a small withholder`
    `not a withholder this month`

GIVEN `withheld in a year ended at least 2 months before` IS A NUMBER, `withheld in a year ended before the month` IS A NUMBER,
      `withheld this month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Withholder size`
`the withholder's size` MEANS
    IF `withheld in a year ended at least 2 months before` GREATER THAN 1000000 THEN `a large withholder`
    ELSE IF `withheld in a year ended before the month` GREATER THAN 25000 THEN `a medium withholder`
         ELSE IF `withheld this month` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `a small withholder`
              ELSE `not a withholder this month`

-- s 16-75(2): a medium withholder pays an amount withheld during a month "by the end of the 21st day of the next month". (2A): a
-- deferred BAS payer, "by the end of the 28th day of: (c) the next month unless the amount is withheld during December; or (d) the
-- next February if the amount is withheld during December."
GIVEN `year withheld` IS A NUMBER, `month withheld` IS A NUMBER, `a deferred BAS payer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the medium withholder's due date` MEANS
    IF `month withheld` EQUALS 12
    THEN IF `a deferred BAS payer` THEN (`year withheld` PLUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS 228 ELSE (`year withheld` PLUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS 121
    ELSE `year withheld` TIMES 10000 PLUS (`month withheld` PLUS 1) TIMES 100 PLUS (IF `a deferred BAS payer` THEN 28 ELSE 21)

-- s 16-75(3): a small withholder pays an amount withheld during a month in a quarter "by the end of the 21st day of the month after
-- the end of that quarter". (4) table, for a deferred BAS payer: quarter ending 30 September -- the following 28 October; 31 December
-- -- the following 28 February; 31 March -- the following 28 April; 30 June -- the following 28 July.
GIVEN `year withheld` IS A NUMBER, `month withheld` IS A NUMBER, `a deferred BAS payer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the small withholder's due date` MEANS
    IF `month withheld` AT MOST 3
    THEN `year withheld` TIMES 10000 PLUS (IF `a deferred BAS payer` THEN 428 ELSE 421)
    ELSE IF `month withheld` AT MOST 6
         THEN `year withheld` TIMES 10000 PLUS (IF `a deferred BAS payer` THEN 728 ELSE 721)
         ELSE IF `month withheld` AT MOST 9
              THEN `year withheld` TIMES 10000 PLUS (IF `a deferred BAS payer` THEN 1028 ELSE 1021)
              ELSE (`year withheld` PLUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS (IF `a deferred BAS payer` THEN 228 ELSE 121)

§§ `s 18-15 -- the recipient's credit`

-- s 18-15(1): "An entity is entitled to a credit equal to the total of the amounts withheld from withholding payments made to the
-- entity during an income year if an assessment has been made of the income tax payable, or an assessment has been made that no
-- income tax is payable".
GIVEN `total withheld in the income year` IS A NUMBER, `an assessment has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the withholding credit` MEANS
    IF `an assessment has been made` THEN `total withheld in the income year` ELSE 0

§§ `ss 45-15, 45-50, 45-60 -- liability for PAYG instalments`

-- s 45-15(1): "The Commissioner may give you an instalment rate from time to time, by giving you written notice of the rate." (2): "You
-- are liable to pay instalments under this Division if the Commissioner has given you an instalment rate." Note 2: "If your
-- assessable income has always consisted wholly of withholding payments ... the Commissioner will not give you an instalment rate."
-- s 45-50(4): liable for a quarter, month or year only if "(a) the Commissioner has given you an instalment rate; and (b) the
-- Commissioner has not withdrawn your instalment rate before the end of that quarter, month or year." Earning business income does
-- not by itself make anyone liable.
GIVEN `the Commissioner has given an instalment rate` IS A BOOLEAN, `the rate has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liable to pay PAYG instalments` IF
    `the Commissioner has given an instalment rate` AND (NOT `the rate has been withdrawn`)

-- s 45-60: the first instalment quarter "consists of the first 3 months of the income year"; the second, the fourth to sixth; the
-- third, the seventh to ninth; the fourth, the tenth to 12th. For an income year ending 30 June: 30 September, 31 December, 31 March
-- and 30 June.
GIVEN `income year ending in` IS A NUMBER, `quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of the instalment quarter` MEANS
    IF `quarter` EQUALS 1 THEN (`income year ending in` MINUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS 930
    ELSE IF `quarter` EQUALS 2 THEN (`income year ending in` MINUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS 1231
         ELSE IF `quarter` EQUALS 3 THEN `income year ending in` TIMES 10000 PLUS 331
              ELSE `income year ending in` TIMES 10000 PLUS 630

§§ `ss 45-125, 45-130, 45-132, 45-134, 45-140, 45-155 -- what kind of payer an individual is`

-- s 45-140(1): you may choose to pay annually "instead of quarterly" if, at the end of the starting instalment quarter, "(a) you are
-- neither registered, nor required to be registered, under Part 2-5 of the GST Act; and (b) you are not a partner in a partnership
-- that is registered, or required to be registered ...; and (c) your most recent notional tax notified by the Commissioner is less
-- than $8,000". ((d) and (e) concern companies; (1A), annual tax period elections, is not modelled.) s 45-155(1)(a): an annual payer
-- stops being one if notified notional tax "is $8,000 or more".
GIVEN `registered or required to be registered for GST` IS A BOOLEAN, `a partner in a GST-registered partnership` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `most recent notional tax notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may choose to pay annually` IF
        (NOT `registered or required to be registered for GST`)
    AND (NOT `a partner in a GST-registered partnership`)
    AND `most recent notional tax notified` LESS THAN 8000

-- s 45-130(1)(a): at the end of the starting instalment quarter, "you are an individual who is not an annual payer, a monthly payer or
-- a quarterly payer who pays on the basis of instalment income" -- a quarterly payer on GDP-adjusted notional tax. s 45-125(1)(b): you
-- may instead "choose to pay quarterly instalments on the basis of your instalment income". s 45-134(1): an individual pays 2
-- instalments (the third and fourth quarters, s 45-50(2)) if (a) carrying on a primary production business whose base-year income
-- exceeded the related deductions, or (b) a special professional whose base-year professional income exceeded the related
-- deductions; otherwise 4 (s 45-132). ss 45-125(5A), 45-130(5): no quarterly status if a monthly payer (s 45-138, an INPUT).
DECLARE `Payer kind` IS ONE OF
    `a monthly payer`
    `an annual payer`
    `a quarterly payer on instalment income`
    `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`
    `a quarterly payer paying 2 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`

DECLARE Individual HAS
    `meets the monthly payer requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered or required to be registered for GST` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a partner in a GST-registered partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
    `most recent notional tax notified` IS A NUMBER
    `chooses to pay annually` IS A BOOLEAN
    `chooses to pay on instalment income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a primary producer with a base-year profit from it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a special professional with a base-year profit from it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `i` IS A Individual
GIVETH A `Payer kind`
`the kind of payer` MEANS
    IF `i`'s `meets the monthly payer requirement` THEN `a monthly payer`
    ELSE IF `i`'s `chooses to pay annually`
            AND `may choose to pay annually` (`i`'s `registered or required to be registered for GST`)
                                             (`i`'s `a partner in a GST-registered partnership`)
                                             (`i`'s `most recent notional tax notified`)
         THEN `an annual payer`
         ELSE IF `i`'s `chooses to pay on instalment income` THEN `a quarterly payer on instalment income`
              ELSE IF `i`'s `a primary producer with a base-year profit from it` OR `i`'s `a special professional with a base-year profit from it`
                   THEN `a quarterly payer paying 2 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`
                   ELSE `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax`

-- s 45-50(1): liable for an instalment quarter if, at its end, a quarterly payer on instalment income or paying 4 instalments on
-- GDP-adjusted notional tax; (2) for "the third or fourth instalment quarter" only, if paying 2; (4) only if the Commissioner has
-- given an instalment rate (not withdrawn). s 45-125(2)(a): the starting instalment quarter is the one in which the rate is given for
-- the first time, "even if it is not the first instalment quarter" -- so no instalment is due for a quarter that ended before the rate
-- was given. Annual and monthly payers pay otherwise (ss 45-50(2A), (3)).
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Payer kind`, `income year ending in` IS A NUMBER, `quarter` IS A NUMBER, `rate first given on` IS A NUMBER,
      `the rate has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liable for the instalment quarter` IF
        `rate first given on` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `rate first given on` AT MOST `the last day of the instalment quarter` `income year ending in` `quarter`
    AND (NOT `the rate has been withdrawn`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the kind`
         WHEN `a quarterly payer on instalment income` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a quarterly payer paying 2 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` THEN `quarter` AT LEAST 3
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `ss 45-61, 45-70 -- when instalments are due`

-- s 45-61(1): a quarterly instalment "is due on or before the 21st day of the month after the end of that quarter". (2): a deferred BAS
-- payer, "(c) the 28th day of the month after the end of that quarter unless all or a part of a December falls within the last month
-- of that quarter; or (d) if all or a part of a December falls within the last month of that quarter--the next 28 February."
GIVEN `income year ending in` IS A NUMBER, `quarter` IS A NUMBER, `a deferred BAS payer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the quarterly instalment due date` MEANS
    IF `quarter` EQUALS 1 THEN (`income year ending in` MINUS 1) TIMES 10000 PLUS (IF `a deferred BAS payer` THEN 1028 ELSE 1021)
    ELSE IF `quarter` EQUALS 2 THEN `income year ending in` TIMES 10000 PLUS (IF `a deferred BAS payer` THEN 228 ELSE 121)
         ELSE IF `quarter` EQUALS 3 THEN `income year ending in` TIMES 10000 PLUS (IF `a deferred BAS payer` THEN 428 ELSE 421)
              ELSE `income year ending in` TIMES 10000 PLUS (IF `a deferred BAS payer` THEN 728 ELSE 721)

-- s 45-70(2): "If the income year ends on 30 June, the [annual] instalment is due on or before the next 21 October."
GIVEN `income year ending in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the annual instalment due date` MEANS
    `income year ending in` TIMES 10000 PLUS 1021

§§ `ss 45-1, 45-110, 45-20, 45-30 -- the amount, notifying instalment income, and the credit`

-- s 45-110(2): the applicable instalment rate is "(a) unless paragraph (b) or (c) applies--the most recent instalment rate given to
-- you by the Commissioner under section 45-15 before the end of that quarter; or (b) if you have chosen an instalment rate for that
-- quarter under section 45-205--that rate"; (c) a rate chosen for an earlier quarter in the year.
GIVEN `the Commissioner's most recent rate` IS A NUMBER, `chose a rate under s 45-205` IS A BOOLEAN, `the chosen rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the applicable instalment rate` MEANS
    IF `chose a rate under s 45-205` THEN `the chosen rate` ELSE `the Commissioner's most recent rate`

-- s 45-110(1): "Work out the amount of an instalment ... as follows" -- THE FORMULA IS MISSING FROM THE DEPOSIT. INFERENCE from the
-- Guide, s 45-1: "you must work out the amount of your quarterly instalment by multiplying your instalment income for an instalment
-- quarter by the rate the Commissioner gave you, or by a rate you choose yourself." Rates are taken as percentages (s 45-320(1): "the
-- percentage worked out to 2 decimal places"). s 45-120(1): instalment income "includes your ordinary income derived during that
-- period, but only to the extent that it is assessable income" -- an INPUT. The GDP-adjusted instalment is the amount the
-- Commissioner works out and notifies (s 45-112(1)(a)) -- an INPUT, not computed.
GIVEN `instalment income for the quarter` IS A NUMBER, `rate in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the quarterly instalment on instalment income` MEANS
    `instalment income for the quarter` TIMES `rate in percent` DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 45-20(1): if liable for an instalment "(even if it is a nil amount), you must notify the Commissioner of the amount of your
-- instalment income". (3): not for "(a) a quarterly instalment worked out under section 45-112 (on the basis of GDP-adjusted notional
-- tax ...); or (b) an annual instalment, unless it is worked out under paragraph 45-115(1)(a) (based on the Commissioner's rate and your
-- instalment income for the income year)."
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Payer kind`, `the annual instalment uses the Commissioner's rate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must notify instalment income` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a quarterly payer paying 4 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a quarterly payer paying 2 instalments on GDP-adjusted notional tax` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an annual payer` THEN `the annual instalment uses the Commissioner's rate`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 45-30(1), (2): on assessment (or a nil assessment), a credit equal to "the total of each instalment payable by you for the income
-- year (even if you have not yet paid it); reduced by: the total of each credit that you have claimed under section 45-215 or 45-420".
GIVEN `instalments payable for the year` IS A NUMBER, `credits claimed under ss 45-215, 45-420` IS A NUMBER,
      `an assessment has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the instalment credit` MEANS
    IF `an assessment has been made` THEN `instalments payable for the year` MINUS `credits claimed under ss 45-215, 45-420` ELSE 0
